{"term":"choke","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:395aa1e597c591f324","definition":"To be unable to breathe because of obstruction of the windpipe (for instance food or other objects that go down the wrong way, or fumes or particles in the air that cause the throat to constrict).","example":"Ever since he choked on a bone, he has refused to eat fish.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee42dce32a3634b8f1","definition":"To prevent (someone) from breathing or talking by strangling or filling the windpipe.","example":"The collar of this shirt is too tight; it’s choking me.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["asphyxiate","strangle","suffocate","throttle"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c9f759843ce3e542b9","definition":"To obstruct (a passage, etc.) by filling it up or clogging it.","example":"to choke a cave passage with boulders and mud","pos":"verb","synonyms":["block up","bung up","clog","congest","jam","obstruct","stop up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fe36415ceefaac5cca","definition":"To hinder or check, as growth, expansion, progress, etc.; to kill (a plant by robbing it of nutrients); to extinguish (fire by robbing it of oxygen).","example":"Now ’tis the spring, and weeds are shallow-rooted;\nSuffer them now, and they’ll o’ergrow the garden\nAnd choke the herbs for want of husbandry.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["choke out","stifle"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0613a4f67cad655710","definition":"To perform badly at a crucial stage of a competition, especially when one appears to be clearly winning.","example":"He has a lot of talent, but he tends to choke under pressure.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7dd87c7d072f8d5c6","definition":"To move one's fingers very close to the tip of a pencil, brush or other art tool.","example":"A brief tryout will demonstrate that the modified grip does indeed make it difficult to “choke” the pencil or apply excessive pressure to the paper.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6cce56d5f14dda3323","definition":"To hold the club or bat lower on the shaft in order to shorten one's swing.","example":"Take a grip with your right hand, slightly choked down from your normal grip.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ba136e5d029b2c74d6","definition":"To be checked or stopped, as if by choking","example":"[…] the words choked in his throat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["stick"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:57f60bf4484f24d4c8","definition":"To check or stop (an utterance or voice) as if by choking.","example":"A hundred times fain he would have spoke, but still his rising Passion choak’d his Words;","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ce6c94bc47974e3a2","definition":"To have a feeling of strangulation in one's throat as a result of passion or strong emotion.","example":"Grobstock began to choke with chagrin.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b8ce64a321a08b099d","definition":"To give (someone) a feeling of strangulation as a result of passion or strong emotion.","example":"[…] I am very sensible how much the Gentlemen of Wit and Pleasure are apt to murmur, and be choqued at the Sight of so many daggled-tail Parsons, who happen to fall in their Way, and offend their Eyes […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f132f06f5b365cc012","definition":"To say (something) with one’s throat constricted (due to emotion, for example).","example":"‘There is the padre!’ Kim choked as bare-headed Father Victor sailed down upon them from the veranda.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:57e20600f78739feed","definition":"To use the choke valve of (a vehicle) to adjust the air/fuel mixture in the engine.","example":"The engine caught, spluttered, and roared as Tom choked the car delicately.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:246a19f7d1dd400bf2","definition":"To reach a condition of maximum flowrate, due to the flow at the narrowest point of the duct becoming sonic (Ma = 1).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:339f3fbdf7ca8d6ba8","definition":"To make or install a choke, as in a cartridge, or in the bore of the barrel of a shotgun.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e31df76